 "full_ledger_sha256": "a22113315436408dcec52fb3024b27503fa0803a53209616061347799c4845e9",
 "note": "In the ledger, `sources` holds indices into `sources` below, and method fields hold indices into `methods`.",
 "methods": [
  "IL: raw GeoJSON odd-even ring containment; no geometry repair or substitution; every own point and record point must lie inside the exact code unit. JM: no boundary computation; separately restricted layer excluded.",
  "Guard only files actually written by SHA-256, each full canonical row, and each field presence/value/type before staging any write. Preserve JSON formatting, key order, newline and every other field. Accept any later HEAD with byte-identical guarded files. Provenance has its own guarded before bytes. Positive --pr replaces event_pr 0 only when applying reviewed events in a selected worktree.",
  "Raw odd-even GeoJSON ring containment, holes respected, exact-edge contacts held; no geometry repair, boundary dissolution, coordinate or point replacement. Jamaican ArcGIS 2022 community geometry has a separate reproduction/redistribution permission restriction: excluded entirely, no geometry computation or population attributes used; all JM rows held for absent admissible boundary proof. CBS 2021 locality boundaries by exact SEMEL_YISH CBS code; service item explicitly subjects use to the same CBS end-user licence. Historical geometry is corroboration, not legal boundary authority or evidence of a different/latest territorial unit.",
  "Require own literal Wikidata item with current P31 and P131 chain to exact stored state, compatible row type/type_local/level/parent_id, and both unchanged row point and own-item point inside raw official boundary. JM: exact unsplit community name, parish and own label with pre-existing locality/community typing. Town/urban-area/neighbourhood/parish scopes remain held. IL: own P3466 CBS code must equal literal locality workbook code, native name, geometry code and official district. No council or district totals, no replacements, and no identity inferred from a name or containment alone.",
  "Owner per-office rule from terms_screen2_v5x: both agencies explicitly permit commercial copying/derived redistribution. Only the screened published STATIN and CBS datasets supply population values. Custom/noncommercial extracts are excluded. Archive exact deciding quotes, original links and dates. Credits disclose selection/reformatting/year and rounding modifications. CBS acknowledgement exception for changed selection/arrangement is quoted; no false assertion of as-is reproduction.",
  "Use immutable unresolved baseline plus later identity events. Any changed unresolved key must retain provable original v4.0 identity and receive a reviewed ordinary classification event, unequal before/after full-row hashes, event_pr 0 and repo compact ledger path/SHA-256. No decision_only. This delivery admits no unresolved keys; all 68 target unresolved keys remain unchanged.",
  "JM: published STATIN Population and Dwelling Counts by Community, Preliminary 2022 Census, reference 12 September 2022; latest public census index still links this table and refreshed body hash matches the archive. Select only the exact own unsplit community cell, excluding parish subtotals and cross-parish parts. IL: CBS August 2026 preliminary estimates, reference 31 August 2026, sheet1 localities of 2,000 or more, H column total persons (not I Israeli-only persons); store Decimal nearest-person ROUND_HALF_UP and retain the literal raw decimal and cell address. Never use council sheets or published geometry population attributes.",
  "Use latest public office release and reference year; stored newer population_year or a dated own-item P1082 claim matching stored population after the selected reference date causes a hold. No source count is inferred from a missing table entry, a regional total, or geometry attributes.",
  "Check every IL stored/own point against OCHA West Bank and Syria reference boundaries and every vertex of the matching raw CBS locality polygon until three positive contacts prove a conservative hold; rows with no contact check all vertices. Raw ring edges are indexed by latitude without alteration; index results match the unindexed method on all stored points. Scope includes East Jerusalem citywide count, Lapid point, and seven border-contact holds; border contacts are uncertainty holds, not jurisdiction claims. Hold all Golan Heights, West Bank or East Jerusalem place identities independently of any count. No disputed-area total is adopted. Every record is either changed with proof, already agreeing, or held; only population and population_year may change."
 ],
